CORE
main.c
--unwindset z_f.0:1 -- --apply-loop-contracts _ --no-standard-checks
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
As in loop_contracts_after_unwinding-01, the do-while(0) loop of z_f is unwound
by a first goto-instrument run, and loop contracts are applied by a second one.
Functions are processed in name order, so a_acq is instrumented before it is
inlined into z_f. Location numbers must be restored before inlining; with stale
location numbers the instrumentation aborted with a precondition failure in
goto_inlinet::add_segment.
